Chapter 6 — Buffer Dynamics

6.1 Buffer ODE

Definition 6.1.

\boxed{\dot{B}_i^k(t) = Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}}(t) + \sum_{j \in S} r_{ji}^k(t) - \sum_{j \in S} r_{ij}^k(t) - z_{ik}(t) - \beta_k B_i^k(t) - R_{ik}(t).}

Assumption 6.1. \beta_k \ge 0, and c_{\mathrm{reg}} \ge 0.

Remark 6.1. The demand term is z_{ik}(t), the delivered rate, consistent with the LP of Chapter 5. The unmet demand d_{ik} - z_{ik} enters \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{MP}} through constraint (v) of Definition 3.5. The regeneration cost R_{ik}(t) couples the buffer ODE to the production dynamics of Chapter 3.

6.2 Viability Constraint

B_i^k(t) \ge B_{i,\min}^k > 0 \quad \forall t.

Definition 6.2 (failure time). \tau_i^k = \inf\{t > 0 : B_i^k(t) < B_{i,\min}^k\}.

6.3 Solutions in Closed Form

Proposition 6.3. If r \equiv 0, R_{ik} \equiv 0, and Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}}, z_{ik} are constant, then

· for \beta_k > 0:

B_i^k(t) = B_i^k(0) e^{-\beta_k t} + \frac{Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}} - z_{ik}}{\beta_k}\big(1 - e^{-\beta_k t}\big);

· for \beta_k = 0:

B_i^k(t) = B_i^k(0) + \big(Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}} - z_{ik}\big) t.

Proof. For \beta_k > 0, integrate the linear ODE \dot{B} + \beta_k B = Q - z with the integrating factor e^{\beta_k t}. For \beta_k = 0, the ODE reduces to \dot{B} = Q - z, whose solution is linear. \square

Corollary 6.4. If \beta_k = 0, Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}} = 0, and z_{ik} is constant and positive, then \tau_i^k = (B_i^k(0) - B_{i,\min}^k)/z_{ik}.

6.4 Blackout Survival

Definition 6.3 (blackout interval). Maximal interval [t_a, t_b] with W_{ij}(t) = 0 for t \in [t_a, t_b] and W_{ij}(t_a^-) = W_{ij}(t_b^+) = 1.

Proposition 6.5 (full-interval condition). Under the hypotheses of Proposition 6.3 with r \equiv 0, R_{ik} \equiv 0, constant Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}} and z_{ik}, node i survives the blackout [t_a, t_b] for function k iff

\boxed{
\min_{t \in [t_a, t_b]} B_i^k(t) \ge B_{i,\min}^k.
}

Because the closed-form B_i^k(t) is monotonic on [t_a, t_b] when Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}} and z_{ik} are constant (its derivative is e^{-\beta_k t}(Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}} - z_{ik} - \beta_k B_i^k(0)), which does not change sign), the minimum is attained at an endpoint:

· if Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}} \ge z_{ik}: minimum at t = t_a;
· if Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}} < z_{ik}: minimum at t = t_b.

For time-varying Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}}(t) or z_{ik}(t), the endpoint condition is not sufficient, and the full-interval condition above must be evaluated.

Remark 6.2. The v1.2 formulation checked only the endpoint t_b. This was correct only under the constant-coefficient assumption and was silent about it. The v1.3 formulation states the assumption explicitly and gives the full-interval condition for the general case.

Remark 6.3. For Mars–Earth medicine, t_b - t_a \approx 26 months (synodic period + transit + occultation). The buffer requirement is thus an output of the ODE, not an assumed constant.

