Chapter 11 — Conclusion

11.1 What We Have Built

A stochastic, constrained, multilayer dynamical system with viability constraints:

\boxed{\text{MCFS} \to \text{Functions} \to \text{Network} \to \text{Flows} \to \text{Buffers} \to \text{Regeneration} \to \text{Cascades} \to \mathcal{V}_{\beta,T}}

The framework makes no assumption about the desirability, optimality, or even existence of any particular multiplanetary configuration. It is designed to test such claims.

11.2 The Central Question

\boxed{\text{When does distributed capacity become civilizational independence?}}

Or, operationally, in terms of the measurable quantity:

\Delta_{\mathrm{MP}}(\rho, \tau_{\mathrm{norm}}, \sigma, \mu) > 0.

11.3 Internal Consistency of v1.3

The eight revisions of this version are mutually reinforcing:

· Deleting (F4) restores the role of buffers as absorbers of blackouts and makes stockpiling matter for H4.
· The slack variable \xi_{ik} makes the LP always feasible, including outside \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{MP}}.
· Removing the intra-node cascade term from Definition 3.7 unifies the cascade in Chapter 7 and eliminates double-counting.
· The buffer cost of regeneration makes H5 a statement about a resourced process and motivates the null-model test.
· Restating cascade convergence on the failure set F aligns the proposition with the actual update rule.
· Replacing \mu_{\mathrm{spec}} by \rho_c = 1 - |\lambda_2(\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{norm}})| yields a non-degenerate connectivity indicator.
· Clarifying the scope of Theorem 2.3′ separates the continuous ODE model (where the theorem applies) from the discrete engine (where it does not, absent regularization).
· Disambiguating \mu, \delta, \lambda removes the symbol collisions that obscured the roles of regeneration, distance, and eigenvalues.

11.4 Next Steps

The next step is not more prose. It is the implementation of the engine of Chapter 9, the execution of the experiments of Chapter 10, and the null-model test of H5. This will determine whether the phase-transition hypothesis survives contact with the equations, and whether the framework earns its keep as a predictive theory rather than a descriptive formalism.

