Appendix B — Full Proofs

B.1 Proposition 2.5 (Knaster–Tarski / Kleene fixed point)

Statement. Let \Phi : \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{N}\times\mathcal{F}) \to \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{N}\times\mathcal{F}) be monotone with respect to inclusion and satisfy \Phi(\emptyset) = \emptyset. Then \Phi has a smallest fixed point containing any given initial failure set F_0, reached in at most |\mathcal{N}|\cdot|\mathcal{F}| iterations of \Phi applied to F_0.

Proof.

Step 1 — Monotonicity of the iterates. Let F_0 \subseteq \mathcal{N}\times\mathcal{F}. Define F_{n+1} = \Phi(F_n). We claim F_0 \subseteq F_1 \subseteq F_2 \subseteq \cdots. Base case: F_0 \subseteq \Phi(F_0) = F_1 is part of the hypothesis on \Phi applied to a cascade map: \Phi(F) \supseteq F for all F \supseteq F_0. Indeed, a cascade map preserves existing failures: \Phi(F) \supseteq F. Assume F_{n-1}\subseteq F_n; then by monotonicity, \Phi(F_{n-1}) \subseteq \Phi(F_n), i.e., F_n \subseteq F_{n+1}.

Step 2 — Stabilization. The lattice \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{N}\times\mathcal{F}) has cardinality 2^{|\mathcal{N}|\cdot|\mathcal{F}|}, but the increasing sequence F_0\subseteq F_1\subseteq\cdots can add at least one element per step (if it has not stabilized). Since there are only |\mathcal{N}|\cdot|\mathcal{F}| elements, the sequence stabilizes after at most |\mathcal{N}|\cdot|\mathcal{F}| strict additions. Let F_\infty = F_{n_0} for the smallest n_0 with F_{n_0+1} = F_{n_0}.

Step 3 — Fixed point. By definition, \Phi(F_\infty) = \Phi(F_{n_0}) = F_{n_0+1} = F_{n_0} = F_\infty. Hence F_\infty is a fixed point containing F_0.

Step 4 — Minimality. Let G be any fixed point of \Phi with G \supseteq F_0. By induction, F_n \subseteq G for all n. Base: F_0 \subseteq G. Step: if F_n \subseteq G, then \Phi(F_n) \subseteq \Phi(G) = G, i.e., F_{n+1} \subseteq G. Hence F_\infty \subseteq G. Therefore F_\infty is the smallest fixed point containing F_0. \square

Corollary B.1. If \Phi is monotone on the complete lattice \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{N}\times\mathcal{F}), the smallest fixed point is the meet of all pre-fixed points:

F_\infty = \bigcap \{G : \Phi(G) \subseteq G,\ G \supseteq F_0\}.

