B.8 Proposition 5.7

Statement. 0\le PI_{\mathrm{dist}}(S,t)\le 1.

Proof. Since D_k \ge 0 and \Delta t\sum_i d_{ik} > 0 for k\in\mathcal{F}^+(S), each ratio is nonnegative. The upper bound follows from Proposition 5.5:

\frac{D_k}{\Delta t\sum_i d_{ik}} \le \frac{\Delta t\sum_i d_{ik}}{\Delta t\sum_i d_{ik}} = 1.

The minimum of ratios in [0,1] lies in [0,1]. \square

