B.9 Proposition 5.8

Statement. PI_{\mathrm{dist}}(S,t)=1 \iff D_k(S,t) = \Delta t\sum_i d_{ik} for all k\in\mathcal{F}^+(S).

Proof.

(\Leftarrow) If D_k = \Delta t\sum_i d_{ik} for all k, each ratio equals 1, so the minimum equals 1.

(\Rightarrow) Suppose PI_{\mathrm{dist}} = 1. Then every ratio is \ge 1. By Proposition 5.7, every ratio is \le 1. Hence every ratio equals 1, i.e., D_k = \Delta t\sum_i d_{ik} for all k. \square

