B.10 Proposition 6.3 (buffer closed form)

Statement. If r\equiv 0, R_{ik}\equiv 0, and Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}}, z_{ik} are constant, then

· for \beta_k > 0: B_i^k(t) = B_i^k(0)e^{-\beta_k t} + \frac{Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}} - z_{ik}}{\beta_k}(1 - e^{-\beta_k t});
· for \beta_k = 0: B_i^k(t) = B_i^k(0) + (Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}} - z_{ik})t.

Proof.

*Case \(\beta_k > 0$.* The ODE is

\dot B + \beta_k B = Q - z.

Multiplying by the integrating factor e^{\beta_k t}:

\frac{d}{dt}(e^{\beta_k t}B) = (Q-z)e^{\beta_k t}.

Integrating from 0 to t:

e^{\beta_k t}B(t) - B(0) = \frac{Q-z}{\beta_k}(e^{\beta_k t} - 1).

Hence

B(t) = B(0)e^{-\beta_k t} + \frac{Q-z}{\beta_k}(1 - e^{-\beta_k t}).

*Case \beta_k = 0$.* The ODE reduces to \(\dot B = Q-z, so B(t) = B(0) + (Q-z)t. \square

