B.17 Empirical margin error bound

Statement. Let \widehat V be a Monte Carlo estimate of V with |\widehat V(C) - V(C)| \le \epsilon uniformly, and |\nabla \widehat V| \ge g_{\min} > 0 on a neighborhood of C. Then

|\widehat{CM}(C) - sCM(C)| \le \frac{\epsilon}{g_{\min}} + O(\epsilon^2).

Proof. Since sCM(C) \approx V(C)/\|\nabla V(C)\| to first order and \widehat{CM}(C) = \widehat V(C)/\|\nabla \widehat V(C)\|, the difference is bounded by

\left|\frac{\widehat V}{\|\nabla\widehat V\|} - \frac{V}{\|\nabla V\|}\right| \le \frac{|\widehat V - V|}{\|\nabla\widehat V\|} + |V|\cdot\left|\frac{1}{\|\nabla\widehat V\|} - \frac{1}{\|\nabla V\|}\right|.

The first term is \le \epsilon/g_{\min}. The second term is O(\epsilon) by Lipschitz continuity of 1/\|\nabla\cdot\| in the gradient. \square

