Appendix E — Numerical Scheme

E.1 Time Discretization

Choose time step \Delta t > 0 and grid points t_n = n\Delta t for n = 0,1,\dots,N_T with N_T = \lceil T/\Delta t\rceil.

Order of operations per step (consistent with Chapter 9):

1. Solve flow LP at t_n: get r^*,z^*,\xi^*.
2. Update buffer: B(t_{n+1}) = B(t_n) + \Delta t\cdot(\text{balance}).
3. Update production via regeneration: Q(t_{n+1}) = Q(t_n) + \Delta t\cdot(\mu(\cdot)_+ - \gamma Q).
4. Apply cascade: Q(t_{n+1}) \leftarrow Q(t_{n+1})\cdot\eta(t_{n+1}).
5. Check constraint set \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{MP}}.
6. Update cumulative unmet demand.

E.2 Stability of the Buffer ODE

Proposition E.1. Under the explicit Euler scheme with step \Delta t, the buffer ODE \dot B = -\beta B + F(t) is stable iff \Delta t < 2/\beta. For unconditional stability, the implicit Euler scheme B_{n+1} = B_n/(1+\beta\Delta t) + \Delta t F_n/(1+\beta\Delta t) is used.

Proof. Explicit Euler: B_{n+1} = B_n(1-\beta\Delta t) + \Delta t F_n. Stability iff |1-\beta\Delta t| < 1, i.e., \Delta t < 2/\beta. Implicit Euler is A-stable for all \Delta t. \square

E.3 Conservation Check

Proposition E.2. In the absence of leakage (\beta_k=0), regeneration cost (c_{\mathrm{reg}}=0), and unmet demand (d_{ik}=z_{ik}), the discrete update conserves total mass:

\sum_i B_i^k(t_{n+1}) = \sum_i B_i^k(t_n) + \Delta t\sum_i Q_{ik}^{\mathrm{prod}}(t_n) - \Delta t\sum_i d_{ik}(t_n).

Proof. Sum the buffer balance over i. The inter-node flow terms cancel by antisymmetry: \sum_i\sum_j r_{ji}^k = \sum_j\sum_i r_{ij}^k. \square

