Appendix I — Conjectures and Open Problems

I.1 Sharp Threshold for H5

Conjecture I.1. There exists a critical regeneration rate \mu_c and a topology-dependent exponent \nu such that

P_{\mathrm{survival}}(\mu) - P_{\mathrm{survival}}(\mu_c) \sim (\mu - \mu_c)^\nu

near the phase transition, for \mu > \mu_c.

Status. Open. Depends on the connectivity of the topology family and the resource cost c_{\mathrm{reg}}.

I.2 Monotonicity of PI_{\mathrm{dist}} in Redundancy

Conjecture I.2. PI_{\mathrm{dist}} is nondecreasing in the number of partially independent nodes, for fixed demand.

Status. Expected but not proved. Counterexamples may exist if redundancy introduces capacity contention.

I.3 Relationship Between \rho_c and \widehat{CM}

Conjecture I.3. For a family of topologies with the same node capacities and demands, \rho_c is positively correlated with \widehat{CM}.

Status. Empirical claim, tested in Experiment 0.

I.4 Closed-Loop Robust Kernel

Conjecture I.4. \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rob}}^{\mathrm{cl}} \subseteq \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rob}}, with strict inclusion whenever the disturbance is not perfectly observable.

Status. Standard result in stochastic control, but the specific form for the MP framework is open.

I.5 Cascade Convergence Rate

Conjecture I.5. The quantitative cascade converges to its fixed point in O(\log(|\mathcal{N}||\mathcal{F}|)) iterations for typical cascade maps, not O(|\mathcal{N}||\mathcal{F}|) as the worst case suggests.

Status. Plausible by analogy with percolation, but not proved.

